<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="03">
<name>Transmission/Transaxle</name>
<section id="1001Y_S000S" variety="S000S">
<name>CVT</name>
<ttl id="1001Y_S000S_744HD_T007Y" variety="T007Y">
<name>CVT System [Super CVT-i] (K112/K112F)</name>
<para id="RM000003RBH009X" category="C" type-id="8048C" name-id="CV09E-10" from="200912">
<dtccode>P0746/62</dtccode>
<dtcname>SL1/DS1 Solenoid Circuit (Performance)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0776/63</dtccode>
<dtcname>SL2/DS2 Solenoid Circuit (Performance)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000003RBH009X_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I8200000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The engine control computer performs shift control by controlling the inflow and outflow of CVT fluid to and from the primary pulley using the shift solenoids (DS1 and DS2).</ptxt>
<ptxt>The engine control computer detects how well the actual gear ratio follows the target gear ratio, and outputs P0746/62 and P0776/63 if it determines that there is a malfunction.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If DTCs for other shift solenoid (DS1 and DS2) circuits) are output at the same time, it is necessary to troubleshoot the DTCs other than P0746/62 and P0776/63 first.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.19in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC NO.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction Duration</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Others</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0746/62</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Starting off or accelerating in D position after engine warm-up</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Not upshifting relative to target gear ratio</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry morerows="3" valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously Variable Transaxle Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Decelerating or stopped in D position after engine warm-up</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Not downshifting relative to target gear ratio</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>1 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0776/63</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Decelerating or stopped in D position after engine warm-up</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Not downshifting relative to target gear ratio</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>1 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Starting off or accelerating in D position after engine warm-up</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Not upshifting relative to target gear ratio</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003RBH009X_02" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003RBH009X_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000003RBH009X_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I8300000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, read the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0746/62 and P0776/63 are output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Codes other than P0746/62 and P0776/63 are also output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003RBH009X_03_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000003RBH009X_03_0005" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003RBH009X_03_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I8400000">
<testtitle>Replace Continuously Variable Transaxle Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the continuously variable transaxle assembly replacement procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000020TJ00AX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003RBH009X_03_0003" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003RBH009X_03_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I8500000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>TaSCAN (A/T / CVT Learned Value Initialization, G Sensor 0-point Learning and CVT Hydraulic Pressure Learning)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Initializing the learned values clears both the G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning values, so when replacing the parts in the table below, be sure to perform both G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning after performing AT/CVT learned value initialization.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Replacement Parts</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously Variable Transaxle Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil Pressure Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After performing AT/CVT learned value initialization, be sure to perform G sensor 0-point learning first, and then CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Be sure to place the vehicle on a level surface and perform 0 point learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not subject the vehicle to vibration while 0 point learning is in progress.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), perform A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021F400AX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs again. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003RBH009X_03_0004" fin="true">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003RBH009X_03_0004">
<testtitle>END</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003RBH009X_03_0005">
<testtitle>Go to the relevant DTC<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000IZJ01JX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>